\par \pard\li175 \fs16\cf1 
\par {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 586L9V}
{\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} 0:Skill Ratings}
\b\fs20 Skill Ratings\plain\fs20\cf1 
\par Bioderms have distinct skills. A list of eight skills is shown beside each one in the Bioderm Facility \uldb \cf2 Biovat\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v BIOVAT}\cf1 : The higher the skill rating, the better. All skills can be increased (at a cost) in \uldb \cf2 VR Training\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 65NO6W}\cf1 .
\par 
\par {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} AGE}
{\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} 0:Age}
\b Age\plain\fs20\cf1 
\par Two numbers show the age and life span of each Bioderm to the left of its picture in the Biovat. Age and life span are measured in years, with a Unitech year equaling ten months.\plain\fs20  \cf1 Bioderms with longer life spans are generally more expensive and have higher overall ratings. All Bioderms start at age zero when they are created. Bioderms that are created, but not linked to a Herc, are cryogenically frozen and do not age between missions. Age is important because every mission requires a predetermined amount of time to complete. After each mission, you will see the remaining life expectancy of each Bioderm that you have linked during the mission debriefing. Make sure they all have enough for the next mission or recycle them in the \uldb \cf2 Medvat\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v .8VUD}\cf1  and replace them with new ones.
\par \pard\li175 
\par {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} HEALTH}
{\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} 0:Health}
\b Health\plain\fs20\cf1 
\par The two numbers show the current health and the potential health of the Bioderm displayed. All Bioderms start completely healthy upon creation. Health deteriorates as a Bioderm\'92s Herc Herc or the Bioderm directly\plain\fs20  \cf1 takes hits during battle.\plain\fs20  \cf1 It will also deteriorate once Toxin levels are maximized. Health can be restored with the \uldb \cf2 Regen\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v REGEN}\cf1  option in the \uldb \cf2 Medvat\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v .8VUD}\cf1 .
\par 
\par {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} KP6J_A}
{\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} 0:Genetic Stability}
\b Genetic Stability\plain\fs20\cf1 
\par The two numbers show the current Genetic Stability and the potential Genetic Stability of the Bioderm displayed. All Bioderms start 100% stable upon creation. Stability deteriorates as a Bioderm\'92s Herc takes hits during battle or as \uldb \cf2 Stimgland\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 4GI42I}\cf1  is administered. Once Genetic Stability reaches half of its maximum, Skill Ratings begin to drop.\plain\fs20  \cf1 Health can be restored with the \uldb \cf2 Regen\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v REGEN}\cf1  option in the \uldb \cf2 Medvat\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v .8VUD}\cf1 .
\par \pard\li175 
\par {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} AOAIRI}
{\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} 0:Toxin Level}
\b Toxin Level\plain\fs20\cf1 
\par The two numbers show the toxin level and the maximum toxin level each Bioderm can sustain. All Bioderms start with zero toxins upon creation. Toxins increase as a Bioderm is infused with \uldb \cf2 StimGland\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 4GI42I}\cf1  while out on missions. Health is affected once the Toxin level is maxed out.\plain\fs20  \cf1 They can be reduced with the \uldb \cf2 Detox\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v DETOX}\cf1  option in the \uldb \cf2 Medvat\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v .8VUD}\cf1 .
\par 
\par }